# R5-1: explicit repository normalization. No renormalization performed; the
# index keeps its current content. This only makes the policy explicit so future
# adds/commits are deterministic and exact-LF source guards stop being fragile.
* text=auto

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF (some Windows tools reject LF-only .cmd/.bat).
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Never normalize these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary

# B4.2a: `decision.ts` is a legacy CRLF file whose committed blob predates the
# `* text=auto` policy above (its blob still holds CR). Editing it therefore used to
# make `git diff --check` report every added line as trailing whitespace, purely because
# of the CR. `cr-at-eol` says the CR is part of the line terminator, so the check reports
# REAL whitespace errors only. The line ending itself is left untouched.
src/orchestration/decision.ts whitespace=cr-at-eol
